# Silvain Aster's camp talks (story/camp_talk.gd). Quest: Aurel's Last Chapter (narrative/companions/aurel.dialogue).

# --- After Strahd called Silvain to kneel at the night visit (strahd/visits:night_kneel) ------------------------------

~ talk_knelt
if name:silvain_aster and flag.strahd_knelt == "silvain_aster"
-> knelt
endif
-> END

~ knelt
Narrator: Silvain is writing by the last of the firelight, small and fast, crossing out almost as much as they keep.
interject name:silvain_aster: He told me I could take notes. So I am. Everything I remember. It comes to half a page. I was there for all of it, and I have half a page.
interject name:silvain_aster: I would like to understand how he did it. I'd like that more than I'd like to sleep, which is probably the point.
* Then study it. Find the weakness. -> knelt_study
* Don't look too closely, Silvain. -> knelt_look

~ knelt_study
interject name:silvain_aster: Already started. He needed my name and my sleep, and nothing else. It's a thin thread. Thin threads cut.
-> END

~ knelt_look
interject name:silvain_aster: Everyone has said that to me about every book I ever wanted. It never once worked.
-> END

~ talk_cipher
if name:silvain_aster and flag.scholar_notes_found and not flag.aurel_cipher_read
-> cipher
endif
-> END

~ cipher
Narrator: Silvain has Aurel's note spread on one knee and a stub of candle at their elbow, and has been reading the same sheet for an hour.
interject name:silvain_aster: Do you know, he wrote in the margins. Tiny. In our shorthand. We invented it in our second year to pass notes during Professor Ostrowe's lectures on comparative moss.
interject name:silvain_aster: I'd forgotten I could still read it. I can. That's either a comfort or the beginning of a very long night.
* What does it say? -> cipher_says
* Comparative moss? -> cipher_moss

~ cipher_moss
interject name:silvain_aster: Four hours a week, for a year. It was the worst year of my life, and the best, because Aurel sat behind me and wrote libels about Ostrowe's beard in the margins of my notes. Where was I.
-> cipher_says

~ cipher_says
interject name:silvain_aster: "Showman at Vallaki asked me the same question I asked him. Knows more than a showman should." Then: "Index at the amber temple. Must see the shape before I read it." And at the bottom: "Going up anyway."
interject name:silvain_aster: He went to the mountains before he came here. Then he came here, and drew the castle's windows, and went up. In that order. He always did his reading backwards.
interject name:silvain_aster: So we follow him backwards. A showman in Vallaki. A temple of amber. I'll want notes.
set aurel_cipher_read
if not (quest.aurels_last_chapter >= the_satchel)
quest aurels_last_chapter the_satchel
endif
if not (quest.aurels_last_chapter >= the_cipher)
quest aurels_last_chapter the_cipher
endif
-> END

~ talk_tome
if name:silvain_aster and quest.find_the_tome == found
-> tome
endif
-> END

~ tome
Narrator: Silvain reads the Tome of Strahd all night, and nobody tries to stop them. Near dawn they go very still, the way a hunting cat goes still.
interject name:silvain_aster: Here. The last pages. Not the history. Notes, in the same hand as the rest, written in last winter's ink.
interject name:silvain_aster: "My reader Mirescu asks again to be allowed to sleep. Denied. He has not finished the chapter. He reads my youth aloud more beautifully than I lived it, and he weeps at the right places. I have not had such an audience in three centuries."
interject name:silvain_aster: He's alive. He's in the castle, in the room with the lamp that never goes out, and he's reading. Still reading.
if flag.eva_question == "aurel"
interject name:silvain_aster: Exactly as that dreadful old woman said. I shall have to tell her she was right. I'd rather be bitten.
endif
* Then we'll go and get him. -> tome_get
* Silvain, he may not be the same man by now. -> tome_same

~ tome_get
interject name:silvain_aster: Yes. Yes, we will. That is the logical course of action. Entirely logical. I'm not crying, the candle smokes.
-> tome_end

~ tome_same
interject name:silvain_aster: I know. I've read the literature on what he keeps and how. I know exactly what I may find in that tower.
interject name:silvain_aster: I'm going anyway. He'd have come for me. He'd have complained about it the whole way, and come.
-> tome_end

~ tome_end
interject name:ilse_varga: East tower. Noted. We take it in daylight, all together, nobody goes ahead.
interject name:hedda_ironvow: Mm. And we bring a lamp. He asked for one.
if not (quest.aurels_last_chapter >= still_reading)
quest aurels_last_chapter still_reading
endif
-> END
